  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of $(x-2)^{4}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{4!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{4!} & =-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{24} & =-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(2) & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
